  "notes": [
    "Van Eeghenstraat 180-212 (pand 0363100012236607, built 1905): a mansard-roofed villa block on the Vondelpark's south edge.",
    "walls[0] south-east villa front (panel 10, 12.2 m; crops w03-155w 2023-01-10 and w03-155L 2019-12-06): red-brown brick over a low souterrain, two storeys of three wide windows with cream hood moulds and keystones, a round central balcony on each floor and a terrace balustrade, a slate mansard with three dormers and an attic row (mansard storeys drawn as slate-coloured stone storeys: the kit has no mansard wall face).",
    "walls[1] was the park front (panel 1, 13.1 m; crop w02-335p 2021-03-26 through bare trees): left to otherWalls (brick grid in the house palette) because its 3DBAG wall rises 1.5 m above the LoD2.2 roof edge (19.0 vs 17.4 m: a parapet in front of a terrace), which the eaves gate refuses; the photo through the trees shows only the brick and three window columns.",
    "INFERRED: walls[1] the north-east side (no photo) and the party, rear and park walls (otherWalls brick grid)."
  ],
